### Monsterbox Maple server endpoints
### Edit @host below to match the device's IP (see boot log / Resolver.Log output for "WiFi connected. IP: ...")
@host = 192.168.1.102:5417

### Info: the prop's name, kind and version as JSON (the remote's subnet scan uses it)
GET http://{{host}}/info

### The sounds on the card and their file numbers, as JSON: [{"number":0,"name":"Werewolf"},...]
### (from the Sounds section of app.config.yaml, which tools\Copy-SoundsToCard.ps1 writes from a folder of sound files)
GET http://{{host}}/sounds

### Play the first sound on the card, file number 0 (returns immediately; plays after the current track ends, replacing any already-pending sound)
POST http://{{host}}/sound?filenumber=0

### Play another sound: use any "number" from GET /sounds above
POST http://{{host}}/sound?filenumber=7

### A missing or non-numeric filenumber is rejected with 400
POST http://{{host}}/sound

### Shake with default configuration (25-50 iterations, 50-75ms delay)
### Responds when the shake finishes (200), or immediately with 409 if a shake is already running
POST http://{{host}}/shake

### Shake with a short, gentle run
POST http://{{host}}/shake?bi=5&ei=10&bd=100&ed=150

### Shake with a long, aggressive run
POST http://{{host}}/shake?bi=40&ei=50&bd=25&ed=40
